Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.37,0:00:05.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Use two dials as a map:\N{\c&H3468EB&}quadrupole{\c&HF7F4F2&} across, dipole up.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.07,0:00:10.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}With the knob low, the state\Ncircles in one whirlpool, and stays.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.19,0:00:15.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}A mirror twin circles the\Nmirror whirlpool: dipole down.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.81,0:00:20.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Each start is trapped.\NThe dipole never changes sign.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.94,0:00:22.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Now turn {\c&H7AAF1B&}Gamma{\c&HF7F4F2&} up.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.72,0:00:28.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Just above zero point eight six, the\Nwhirlpools touch: a narrow corridor opens.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.44,0:00:35.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}The state lingers on one side,\Nthen slips through. The {\c&H3468EB&}dipole{\c&HF7F4F2&} flips.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.32,0:00:40.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Nothing here is random. So,\Nwill the flips come like clockwork?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.34,0:00:46.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}No. Long waits and\Nshort ones, irregularly.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.27,0:00:51.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}The dipole's sign prints uneven\Nstripes, like the seafloor.
